[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,1.60) {Sunflower};
\foreach \x in {0.00} {\draw[fill=blue!15] (\x,1.30) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.95) {Millet};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70} {\draw[fill=red!12] (\x,0.65) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.1,0.30) {Wheat};
\foreach \x in {0.00,0.70,1.40,2.10,2.80,3.50,4.20,4.90,5.60} {\draw[fill=green!20] (\x,0.00) rectangle +(0.7,0.6);}
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,amplitude=5pt}] (6.55,1.90)--(6.55,0) node[midway,right=8pt,font=\small] {$60$ kg};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Bird seed is mixed from sunflower, millet and wheat in the ratio $1:2:9$.
How much wheat is in a $60$ kg batch?
